1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--typing-practice","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/typing-practice","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/typing-practice","sourceHash":"e1093b1bca9708e37b60c4ba1275e57c0fc7a74be1c3e68368d9a18a0c8cb3e7","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:20.148Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Typing Practice","zh":"打字练习"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If your target language uses a different keyboard layout, script, or character set, you'll need dedicated practice to build typing speed. Even if the script is the same (like a Spanish speaker learning English), the letter combinations are different and your fingers need to learn them.","zh":"如果你的目标语言使用不同的键盘布局、文字系统或字符集，你需要进行专门练习来提升打字速度。即使文字系统相同（例如西班牙语使用者学习英语），字母组合也不同，你的手指需要学会新的组合方式。"}},{"id":"why-it-matters","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Matters","zh":"为什么重要"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Writing practice only works if the physical act of typing isn't a bottleneck. If you can only type 5 words per minute, you'll spend all your mental energy on finding keys instead of thinking about the language.","zh":"只有在打字这一身体动作不会成为瓶颈时，写作练习才有效。如果你每分钟只能打5个词，你的全部精力都会花在寻找按键上，而不是思考语言。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Aim for at <em>least</em> 25 words per minute before moving on from Phase 5A.","zh":"在结束阶段5A之前，目标是达到<em>至少</em>每分钟25个词。"}},{"id":"how-to-practice","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Practice","zh":"练习方法"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Choose to focus on either a physical keyboard OR mobile keyboard. Learn one, then move on to the other","zh":"选择专注于实体键盘或移动键盘中的一种。先学会一种，再练习另一种"},{"en":"Use typing practice websites (many exist for specific languages)","zh":"使用打字练习网站（许多网站针对特定语言设计）"},{"en":"Copy texts that already exist rather than trying to compose your own","zh":"复制已有的文本，而不是尝试自己创作"},{"en":"Depending on the language, you may need to learn a very new way of typing (Chinese or Japanese have very different methods than European languages)","zh":"根据语言不同，你可能需要学习一种全新的打字方式（中文或日文的输入方式与欧洲语言非常不同）"},{"en":"You do not need to buy a physical keyboard that matches the target language. All modern computers allow you to add new input methods via settings","zh":"你不需要购买与目标语言匹配的实体键盘。所有现代电脑都允许你通过设置添加新的输入法"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"提示"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"10 minutes of dedicated typing practice per day adds up fast","zh":"每天进行10分钟专门的打字练习，很快就会积少成多"},{"en":"Set up your keyboard with the target language input method and switch between them (standard hotkey is <code>Command + Space</code>)","zh":"将键盘设置为目标语言输入法，并在输入法之间切换（标准快捷键是<code>Command + Space</code>）"},{"en":"If you're moderately techy, consider setting up your own custom keyboard input. Most foreign keyboards also change the position of characters like # or % or ! Relearning these is rather annoying and you likely will never need to use another person's keyboard","zh":"如果你比较熟悉技术，可以考虑设置自己的自定义键盘输入。大多数外语键盘还会改变#、%或!等字符的位置。重新学习这些位置相当烦人，而且你可能永远都不需要使用别人的键盘"},{"en":"If handwriting is important for you personally, see handwriting practice","zh":"如果手写对你个人很重要，请参阅手写练习"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
